{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/40673-crossover-mania","id":40673,"title":"Crossover Mania","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T13:10:48-08:00","id":40673,"title":"Crossover Mania","content":"I'm gearing up for two Vampire (Blood &amp; Smoke) and Mortals parallel/crossover games with elements from Changeling, Book of Spirits, and Hunter, and light touches from Werewolf and potentially Promethean. Over the last few years I've gotten a handle on how to crossover VtR, WtF, CtL, and HtV effectively and in general the power levels and weaknesses aren't too far off from each other.<br /> <br /> Ever since Geist came out, though, I've been kind of wary of more recent releases. It feels like later nWoD lines suffer from &quot;power creep.&quot; Sin-Eaters feel like Swiss Army knives as they gain XP, which is a shame because the theming and atmosphere of the game is so good at early levels. I haven't spent enough time with Mummy or Demon to know if this is true for these lines, but I'd like to be able to introduce Angels/Demons in the later stages of my game. Flipping through the Quickstart, I'm getting the same Swiss Army knife vibe again and I'm not seeing any specific weaknesses other supernaturals or hunters can exploit. Aggro damage from holy water? Weakness on hallowed ground? Something? Between fire, silver, cold iron, what I like about the early games is the chess game of physical, mental, and social combat you could to play across lines.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely like to be wrong! So if anyone has done any crossovers or introduced other supernaturals to a Demon game, please share your experiences and your thoughts on both game balance and on how it felt in terms of story and theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1872-kinowolf","name":"Kinowolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T13:45:30-08:00","id":40712,"title":"","content":"The thing about Demons is that they get their own personal weaknesses as they grow stronger or have unresolved disagreements with reality, and they're called glitches. Now, most of them are not allergies like fire/sun to Vampires, cold iron to the fae, etc... but they can be.<br /> Demons have another sort of weakness that can be exploited, though, and it's their Cover. You might not be able to kill them directly easily (given they can burn off their Cover in the worst case and make you eat your own teeth). But you can shatter their human disguise, which is very precious to them. Investigate it, poke the holes, advertise the inconsistencies and oddities. And the beauty is, the lower the Cover, the more fragile it is, as it's accompanied with its own unnatural phenomena. And when a Demon has no human disguise left? It's likely to be picked up by its old boss. Therefore, if you get it right, you'll never have to physically fight a Demon yourself, yet be feared among them. When vampires, werewolves, and others have their disguise threatened, they can try to kill you on time and avoid suffering any fallout, whereas once a Demon's Cover has been damaged, killing the witness won't bring it back to its previous level, even if he doesn't have the time to tell anyone else; and even if their mundane identity is destroyed, most monsters can still pass as human, whereas Demons can't.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents on the weakness of Demons. There's more than you think. In a way, Demons can be weaker then most other supernaturals because a single unarmed stalker is able to destroy their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:05:38-08:00","id":40723,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I think the hard think to grok is that, with Demon's primary weakness manifested through the God-Machine coming after them, it's more narrative than a simple bane of Fire or Silver, and requires their opponents to really unravel the mystery. You discover their identity and all the problems with it and you expose its weakness. When it's fighting Angels and Cultists, you either help them finish the job or maybe try to blow both to high heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:10:44-08:00","id":40725,"title":"","content":"As an aside, a Demon in their Cover is\u2014barring certain Embeds\u2014just as squishy as any other mortal.<br /> For your perusal, the 98% complete draft they posted on <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">the Kickstarter</a>:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7F...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Note: the Cacaphonic Embed, On the Mend has been modified as follows:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Wits + Medicine</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Action: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Roll Results </span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Dramatic Failure: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The character fails to heal the target, and in fact makes the injury heal unpredictably. Whenever the target would heal a point of damage (every 15 minutes for bashing, 2 days for lethal, etc.), the target\u2019s player rolls Stamina. If the roll succeeds, the wound heals. If it fails, the wound does not heal. On a dramatic failure, the wound worsens (the character suffers one additional wound of the same type). This cycle ceases if the character gets professional medical care. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Failure: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The demon fails to heal the target. Further attempts to use this Embed on the same target suffer a cumulative \u20131 penalty. This penalty goes away once the target has fully healed. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><b>Success:</b> Choose one: All of the target\u2019s bashing damage heals in fifteen minutes, or all of the target\u2019s lethal damage heals overnight, or all of the target\u2019s aggravated damage changes to lethal. A given target can only benefit from one use of On the Mend at a time, meaning that if the demon uses the Embed to change aggravated damage to lethal, she cannot then use the Embed to speed the target\u2019s healing of the lethal damage. Healing a normal human being of aggravated or lethal damage causes a compromise roll, and therefore demons are often loathe to do so. The demon can use this Embed on herself. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> As above, except the options are as follows: Target heals all bashing damage; target heals all lethal damage in an hour; target heals one point of aggravated damage per success or per dot of the demon\u2019s Primum, whichever is lower </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  added clarifying commas. 01-01-2014, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T18:54:20-08:00","id":40883,"title":"","content":"This is all good stuff! I hadn't considered that the Covers could take permanent &quot;damage&quot; in this way. Theoretically, a vampire could take a demon on in public and be at a big advantage. If the demon converts into his demon form to survive, he doesn't have the benefit of lunacy clouding witnesses like a werewolf in hybrid form does. His Cover will be dinged and the vampire could then retreat. Mix in some stalking, as you guys have pointed out, and you've got an effective guerrilla takedown. In some ways they're more vulnerable than werewolves in their &quot;war form.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't much like the &quot;boogeyman comes for you if you stand out&quot; style of weakness, so the God Machine threat is less compelling to me. There's too much deus ex machina (hur hur) to it. But losing Cover in and of itself, like losing Humanity or Harmony, seems like a big deal mechanically. I like the idea that if you harass a demon it'll either fight back under Cover (basically as a Mortal) or use its Exploits and Demon Form until it glitches out and loses the ability to function. I also hadn't considered that demons wouldn't have access to something like the Regeneration Numen that angels and spirits can easily get.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any specific Chronicle stories of introducing demons to another game line or other supernaturals to a Demon game? I would like to hear how different sessions played out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1872-kinowolf","name":"Kinowolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:20:03-08:00","id":41152,"title":"","content":"Also fun to remember, a vampire engaging a demon with an understanding of 'How Cover Works' never needs to even get -close- to the Unchained. They can just investigate them from afar until repeated compromises force them to abandon whatever identity they have.<br /> <br /> If you understand Demons, you can -always- drive them away, simply by pulling the threads on the sweater they wear to your identity party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:37:00-08:00","id":41295,"title":"","content":"As far as Mummies go, they are also pretty powerful, but not QUITE as all purpose as an advanced Sin-Eater. Mummies also START the game at tier absurd power levels, but quickly hemorrhage power. IIRC theorycraft on the Mummy forum says a mummy can AT BEST pull 260ish days for their full descent, and that's assuming EVERY descent roll goes their way. On average, outside of a Sothic Turn, a Mummy has a run of 60-75 days even if they ARE following their purpose, and about 50 days of that are power 3 or less.<br /> <br /> So, dropping a Starting Mummy (Sekhem 8-10) into a game with a starting Vampire/Werewolf/Mage/Etc (Power Stat 1-3) is pretty broken, but dropping a Sekhem 1-3 Mummy into a game give the mummy like a month before it falls dormant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T14:59:45-08:00","id":41347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/40673-crossover-mania?p=41295#post41295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Mummies go, they are also pretty powerful, but not QUITE as all purpose as an advanced Sin-Eater. Mummies also START the game at tier absurd power levels, but quickly hemorrhage power. IIRC theorycraft on the Mummy forum says a mummy can AT BEST pull 260ish days for their full descent, and that's assuming EVERY descent roll goes their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two years and two-hundred fifty days, going by the non-narrative time units and assuming only scheduled Descent rolls, every one of which fails until the target number for success is reduced to 1. You add seven times the added length for failure to the initial timer.<br /> <br /> All this is assuming that no resets are made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On average, outside of a Sothic Turn, a Mummy has a run of 60-75 days even if they ARE following their purpose, and about 50 days of that are power 3 or less. </div> </div> </div>Once you've dropped to Sekhem 7 the duration starts extending dramatically. Even if they completed their First Purpose already and thus automatically succeeded every Descent roll from then to completion they'd still have about thirteen months of activity left, the first nine or ten weeks of which are above Sekhem 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-02-2014, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T01:44:48-08:00","id":41582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/40673-crossover-mania?p=41152#post41152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also fun to remember, a vampire engaging a demon with an understanding of 'How Cover Works' never needs to even get -close- to the Unchained. They can just investigate them from afar until repeated compromises force them to abandon whatever identity they have.<br /> <br /> If you understand Demons, you can -always- drive them away, simply by pulling the threads on the sweater they wear to your identity party.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem only begins when a demon feels threatened and especially if he finds out who is behind it. He can then easily turn tables there if he is primum 2+.<br /> He can press other ppl into soulpacts with him and switch throguh covers quickly to find a trace of who gets into his way.<br /> <br /> As example: The demon found out that a private investigator has been researching into his cover over and over again now. Suddenly that ones wife gets asked questions by the neighbours kid.<br /> Then by the mail guy. Even the investigator himself gets asked by them. Then even his wife asks him about the case he is on all of a sudden and acts strangely.<br /> <br /> Then as soon as he spills something he has a strange smile when he meets up with his client the next time.<br /> <br /> (first three pressed into a soul pact or tricked and the last one got with the promise of giving his wife back to him [not standing on the pact though]).<br /> <br /> That only as an example. If a demon gets cornered he will switch through as many covers as possible to get near who has threatened him and do something about the problem (pointing that guy to an enemy, the GM or the next vampire with wrong infos if he is mean, or do something himself about the problem if he is more a fighter type)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:03:48-08:00","id":41758,"title":"","content":"I dunno about you, but in my games, my players don't exactly have 'Covers to Burn' persay.<br /> <br /> I mean, they get new ones, but they're pretty precious resources.<br /> <br /> Burner covers are a good idea in theory but in practice they 'burn' really, really quick.<br /> <br /> Cover is a harsh system but it's supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T15:13:33-08:00","id":41973,"title":"","content":"The GM weakness isn't as deus ex machina as it comes across as. Cover does represent it in an integrity loss sense, and compromise roles do impose conditions that represent the watchful eye of god more concretely. like other conditions, they have side effects and resolution actions. those will put a burden on the demon, forcing him to be more careful and less bold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T16:03:22-08:00","id":42007,"title":"","content":"My biggest question would be what role do you want the Unchained to have in your story? Are they antagonists? Potential allies? Just background set dressing somehow? How would your PC's (presumably mortals and/or vampires) notice demons in the first place? What are the circumstances?<br /> <br /> Answering those questions will go a long way to formulating a response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T01:48:08-08:00","id":42180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/40673-crossover-mania?p=42007#post42007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest question would be what role do you want the Unchained to have in your story? Are they antagonists? Potential allies? Just background set dressing somehow? How would your PC's (presumably mortals and/or vampires) notice demons in the first place? What are the circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. The overarching metaplot of the game revolves around a) Strix, and b) the Archangel Vahishtael (from the Testament of Longinus). In my version of WoD, Vahishtael's duty to the God Machine is to deal with errors in the death cycle (i.e. undeath). That mission is open-ended, and the archangel is just as likely to attempt to integrate errors as to remove them, which is why he's appeared to Kindred with messages. I've also tied in a lot of Underworld and ghost material. My Strix originally escaped from the deepest part of the Underworld, the Darkness Before Death. They are manifestations of that pure, entropic energy. They didn't create vampires per se, but they created the Beast that links each clan together (technically, they are the Beast). etc. etc.<br /> <br /> You can see where I'm overlapping vampires, angels, ghosts, and Strix. Later in the game the players could be dealing with powerful Strix, angels, and potentially demons. They could be antagonists or allies, depending on how things play out. I could strip them down into set dressing and use modified rules for angels, but I want to at least explore the idea of including the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1872-kinowolf","name":"Kinowolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}